ace authorization reuses the existing auth plugin infrastructure\n  (Staff Engineer input: SSAR detail is over-specified at strategy level).\n- Keep the authentication layer (`--app-name kubernetes-auth`, kube-rbac-proxy sidecar)\n  unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Workspace resolution succeeds in the artifacts-only server context without tracking store\n  or model registry store initialization, demonstrated by a passing test exercising the\n  `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point in that context.\n- The tracking server's non-artifact workspace resolution behavior is unchanged\n  (regression tests pass).\n- No changes are made to the authentication setup or the plugin's registration mechanism.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-7 (P1): auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only\n  context without tracking store initialization — direct coverage.\n- Enables HLR-1, HLR-2, HLR-3 (P0): the server-side workspace validation calls this\n  resolution; this epic therefore inherits P0 by priority inheritance.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The plugin has no dedicated architecture-context file; its current initialization path is\n  strategy-asserted and validated by the gating investigation. If the refactor is larger\n  than the single sprint estimated in the strategy, re-plan the server-side epic's start\n  date accordingly.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":81840,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc9990585c0fc227","agent_id":"a9ee74de494750547","session_id":"40ac0a95-f7b4-4f3c-bf55-b2c4e97b3f62","uuid":"173a8556-d3e0-43e9-8c1c-86858a152083","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:22:16.451Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
