 selected routing mechanism with rationale,\n  covering both the main tracking deployment's routing configuration and the dedicated\n  instance's HTTPRoute design.\n- The document states definitively whether the tracking server needs a configuration\n  change to delegate artifact operations (branch selection), so downstream scope is\n  unambiguous.\n- The design is consistent with the operator's Helm-in-operator pattern and conditional\n  Gateway API CRD discovery.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated\n  artifacts-only instance — this investigation determines that requirement's design.\n- HLR-5 (P1): informs the HTTPRoute design of the dedicated instance deployment.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":83836,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc9990585c0fc227","agent_id":"a9ee74de494750547","session_id":"40ac0a95-f7b4-4f3c-bf55-b2c4e97b3f62","uuid":"50b08a71-6f7f-41e1-bda8-9fb160766c51","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:22:38.731Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
