ifact serving enabled, the rendered operator\n  configuration routes artifact traffic from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated\n  artifacts-only instance, per the mechanism selected by the routing-design investigation.\n- The routing configuration is rendered declaratively from the MLflow CR (no\n  manually-managed intermediate resources).\n- Artifact requests entering through the main tracking deployment's ingress reach the\n  dedicated artifacts-only instance and are subject to its workspace validation, verified\n  end-to-end once the dedicated instance deployment and the workspace-aware server\n  capability are available.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated\n  artifacts-only instance — direct coverage (together with the conditional server-side\n  delegation work if the routing-design investigation selects that branch).\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The implementation surface depends on the routing-design outcome; this epic is gated by\n  that investigation with a rewrite impact.\n- Coordination with the dedicated-instance deployment work is required where both modify\n  the operator's Helm chart (merge-conflict risk, not a dependency).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":85312,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc9990585c0fc227","agent_id":"a9ee74de494750547","session_id":"40ac0a95-f7b4-4f3c-bf55-b2c4e97b3f62","uuid":"e3545a42-87a0-43bb-b0b6-48fed3e5adad","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:22:59.392Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
