{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1b1889389019f9c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n3\ttitle: Validate artifact-path-to-workspace resolvability in the artifacts-only server\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 1\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Validate artifact-path-to-workspace resolvability in the artifacts-only server\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves the strategy assumption that artifact request paths carry\n30\tsufficient information (experiment ID or run ID) to resolve workspace membership in the\n31\tartifacts-only server, and the associated risk that artifact paths may not straightforwardly\n32\tmap to experiment IDs across artifact storage backends or custom artifact root\n33\tconfigurations. The server's design resolves each artifact path to its parent experiment\n34\t(artifacts stored under experiment-scoped paths such as\n35\t`{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/`), looks up the experiment's workspace assignment via\n36\tthe workspace store, and delegates authorization to the existing auth plugin\n37\tinfrastructure. If the paths do not resolve, the server-side approach must be redesigned\n38\tbefore implementation proceeds.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Analyze the artifact request endpoints (`/api/2.0/mlflow/artifacts/*`) and the\n43\t  artifacts-only proxy's request path handling in the MLflow server to determine what\n44\t  identity (experiment ID, run ID) is recoverable from each request.\n45\t- Confirm the path-to-experiment mapping for the S3 artifact store (the standard RHOAI\n46\t  configuration) where paths follow the `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/` structure.\n47\t- Document limitations for non-standard artifact roots and other storage backends, per the\n48\t  strategy's risk mitigation (initial implementation scoped to the S3 artifact store).\n49\t- Identify initialization-sequence interactions between `--artifacts-only` and\n50\t  `--enable-workspaces` when used individually, to confirm the flags can be made composable\n51\t  without breaking either flag's standalone behavior.\n52\t- Deliver a findings document confirming or refuting path-to-workspace resolvability, with\n53\t  the concrete resolution mechanism for the S3-scoped layout.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- A findings document states definitively whether artifact request paths in the\n58\t  artifacts-only server resolve to experiment (and therefore workspace) identity for the\n59\t  S3 artifact store layout, citing the endpoints and path structures examined.\n60\t- Limitations for non-standard artifact roots and non-S3 backends are documented.\n61\t- Initialization-sequence constraints on combining `--artifacts-only` with\n62\t  `--enable-workspaces` are identified and recorded for the server implementation.\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- HLR-1 (flag composability) and HLR-2 (workspace validation of artifact requests): this\n67\t  investigation determines the feasibility and mechanism of the server's\n68\t  path-to-workspace resolution approach.\n69\t- Supports HLR-3 (fail-closed) and HLR-4 (backwards compatibility) scoping.\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5c1588c5161e57b","agent_id":"a5a85d92803f72756","session_id":"40ac0a95-f7b4-4f3c-bf55-b2c4e97b3f62","uuid":"2640a73d-5108-4144-a5e5-9af1d70c64a0","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:26:31.427Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1b1889389019f9c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
