{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8fe87a2a836b315a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n3\ttitle: Extend mlflow-kubernetes-plugins workspace resolution for the artifacts-only\n4\t  context\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n6\tcomponent: MLflow\n7\tteam: MLflow Team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the plugin's workspace resolution is already decoupled from\n16\t    tracking store initialization, this epic reduces to verification and regression\n17\t    coverage; if it is coupled, workspace resolution is factored into an independent\n18\t    initialization path within the plugin per the investigation's refactor plan.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 5\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Extend mlflow-kubernetes-plugins workspace resolution for the artifacts-only context\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tThis epic makes the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` auth plugin's workspace resolution function\n41\tcorrectly in the artifacts-only server context, where tracking stores and model registry\n42\tstores are not initialized. The plugin already provides experiment-to-workspace mapping for\n43\tthe tracking server's non-artifact operations through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry\n44\tpoint group; this epic verifies that resolution in the artifacts-only context and, if it is\n45\tcoupled to the full tracking server initialization path, factors workspace resolution into\n46\tan independent initialization path within the plugin. The scope of this epic (verification\n47\tonly vs. refactor) is determined by the plugin initialization-dependency investigation. The\n48\tkube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth` authentication setup are unchanged\n49\t— authentication at the ingress level works identically for both server types.\n50\t\n51\t## Scope\n52\t\n53\t- Verify workspace resolution in an artifacts-only-style context (tracking and model\n54\t  registry stores uninitialized), per the investigation findings.\n55\t- If resolution is coupled to full server initialization: refactor the plugin so workspace\n56\t  resolution has an independent initialization path, preserving the existing entry-point\n57\t  and registry-loading mechanisms.\n58\t- Preserve existing plugin behavior for the tracking server's non-artifact operations\n59\t  (regression scope).\n60\t- Do not prescribe or change Kubernetes API authorization mechanics (SelfSubjectAccessReview\n61\t  or otherwise) — workspace authorization reuses the existing auth plugin infrastructure\n62\t  (Staff Engineer input: SSAR detail is over-specified at strategy level).\n63\t- Keep the authentication layer (`--app-name kubernetes-auth`, kube-rbac-proxy sidecar)\n64\t  unchanged.\n65\t\n66\t## Acceptance Criteria\n67\t\n68\t- Workspace resolution succeeds in the artifacts-only server context without tracking store\n69\t  or model registry store initialization, demonstrated by a passing test exercising the\n70\t  `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point in that context.\n71\t- The tracking server's non-artifact workspace resolution behavior is unchanged\n72\t  (regression tests pass).\n73\t- No changes are made to the authentication setup or the plugin's registration mechanism.\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t- HLR-7 (P1): auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only\n78\t  context without tracking store initialization — direct coverage.\n79\t- Enables HLR-1, HLR-2, HLR-3 (P0): the server-side workspace validation calls this\n80\t  resolution; this epic therefore inherits P0 by priority inheritance.\n81\t\n82\t## Risks / Notes\n83\t\n84\t- The plugin has no dedicated architecture-context file; its current initialization path is\n85\t  strategy-asserted and validated by the gating investigation. If the refactor is larger\n86\t  than the single sprint estimated in the strategy, re-plan the server-side epic's start\n87\t  date accordingly.\n88\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5c1588c5161e57b","agent_id":"a5a85d92803f72756","session_id":"40ac0a95-f7b4-4f3c-bf55-b2c4e97b3f62","uuid":"326362df-6f1d-4135-a943-ed0cc28d01ac","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:26:35.655Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8fe87a2a836b315a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
