{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-93940450c5ea4c95","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n3\ttitle: Determine split-server artifact traffic routing design\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Determine split-server artifact traffic routing design\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves the strategy's open question: how should the MLflow operator\n30\tconfigure artifact traffic routing from the main tracking server to the dedicated\n31\tartifacts-only instance? The answer affects the HTTPRoute design for the dedicated instance\n32\tand determines whether the tracking server needs a configuration change to delegate\n33\tartifact operations. The outcome selects between two bounded branches: (A) gateway-level\n34\trouting (HTTPRoute path-based routing) suffices and no tracking-server change is needed, or\n35\t(B) the tracking server additionally needs a configuration change to delegate artifact\n36\toperations, which would be planned as conditional follow-up work.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Evaluate Gateway API HTTPRoute routing options for splitting artifact traffic from the\n41\t  main tracking deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, consistent with the\n42\t  operator's existing conditional CRD discovery pattern for Gateway API resources.\n43\t- Determine whether the main tracking deployment needs configuration changes (or the\n44\t  tracking server needs a delegation capability) for artifact traffic to reach the\n45\t  dedicated instance correctly.\n46\t- Define the HTTPRoute design implications for the dedicated artifacts-only instance's own\n47\t  ingress.\n48\t- Record the decision, the selected routing mechanism, and the branch outcome (A or B) with\n49\t  rationale, as the input to the operator topology implementation work and the strategy's\n50\t  to-be-created design doc.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- A design decision document records the selected routing mechanism with rationale,\n55\t  covering both the main tracking deployment's routing configuration and the dedicated\n56\t  instance's HTTPRoute design.\n57\t- The document states definitively whether the tracking server needs a configuration\n58\t  change to delegate artifact operations (branch selection), so downstream scope is\n59\t  unambiguous.\n60\t- The design is consistent with the operator's Helm-in-operator pattern and conditional\n61\t  Gateway API CRD discovery.\n62\t\n63\t## HLR Traceability\n64\t\n65\t- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated\n66\t  artifacts-only instance — this investigation determines that requirement's design.\n67\t- HLR-5 (P1): informs the HTTPRoute design of the dedicated instance deployment.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5c1588c5161e57b","agent_id":"a5a85d92803f72756","session_id":"40ac0a95-f7b4-4f3c-bf55-b2c4e97b3f62","uuid":"4e472570-cc9c-4c19-839b-415437ad2d4d","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:26:39.360Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-93940450c5ea4c95","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
