{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a91baeab8b45d5a0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E010\n3\ttitle: End-to-end integration validation of workspace-aware split-server artifact\n4\t  serving\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n6\tcomponent: MLflow\n7\tteam: MLflow Team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P1\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E004\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E006\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E007\n14\tai_signals:\n15\t  change_specificity: 1\n16\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n17\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n18\t  existing_foundation: 1\n19\t  open_questions: 0\n20\t  external_dependency: 1\n21\t  human_process_gates: 0\n22\t  repo_access: 1\n23\t  architecture_claims: 1\n24\timplementation_type: null\n25\tinvestigation_signals: null\n26\tai_implementability: High\n27\tai_implementability_score: 7\n28\tjira_key: null\n29\tbranch: null\n30\tgated_by: null\n31\tgate_failure_impact: null\n32\t---\n33\t# End-to-end integration validation of workspace-aware split-server artifact serving\n34\t\n35\t## Description\n36\t\n37\tThis epic delivers the cross-component integration validation called out in the strategy's\n38\teffort estimate: multi-tenant workspace scenarios, backwards compatibility and\n39\tsingle-tenant regression, fail-closed edge cases, and split-server routing, executed\n40\tagainst the operator-deployed split-server topology (dedicated artifacts-only instance with\n41\tworkspace validation, main tracking deployment routing artifact traffic to it). The\n42\tserver-level behaviors carry their own acceptance scenarios in the server work; this epic\n43\tvalidates the combined, operator-deployed system.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Multi-tenant workspace scenarios against the operator-deployed topology: workspace member\n48\t  receives artifacts (HTTP 200 with correct content); non-member denied (HTTP 403);\n49\t  workspace store unreachable denied (HTTP 503, fail-closed).\n50\t- Single-tenant and no-workspace-flags regression: deployments without `--enable-workspaces`\n51\t  retain current artifact serving behavior end-to-end.\n52\t- Split-server routing validation: artifact traffic entering through the main tracking\n53\t  deployment's ingress reaches the dedicated artifacts-only instance and is subject to\n54\t  workspace validation; non-artifact operations (tracking, model registry, prompt registry)\n55\t  continue to be served by the main tracking deployment.\n56\t- Test infrastructure and scenarios reusable for regression (consistent with the existing\n57\t  operator test tooling).\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- The multi-tenant scenario suite passes against the operator-deployed split-server\n62\t  topology: member access serves artifacts (200), cross-workspace access is denied (403),\n63\t  and workspace-store unavailability denies requests (503).\n64\t- The single-tenant / no-workspace-flags regression suite passes: current behavior is\n65\t  preserved end-to-end.\n66\t- Artifact requests through the main tracking deployment's ingress are served by the\n67\t  dedicated artifacts-only instance with workspace validation enforced, and non-artifact\n68\t  operations are unaffected.\n69\t- The scenarios are committed as reusable regression tests.\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- HLR-5 (P1), HLR-6 (P1): end-to-end verification of the operator-deployed split-server\n74\t  topology and artifact traffic routing — primary mapping.\n75\t- Regression coverage for HLR-1 through HLR-4 (P0): the server-level acceptance scenarios\n76\t  for those requirements are verified within the server work; this epic re-verifies them\n77\t  in the integrated topology.\n78\t\n79\t## Risks / Notes\n80\t\n81\t- This epic is P1: its gating deliverable is verification of the P1 operator topology. The\n82\t  P0 server behaviors carry their own acceptance scenarios in the server work; labeling\n83\t  this epic P0 would force the P1 operator epics to P0 through priority inheritance.\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5c1588c5161e57b","agent_id":"a5a85d92803f72756","session_id":"40ac0a95-f7b4-4f3c-bf55-b2c4e97b3f62","uuid":"ad47f08e-da23-4ce9-86da-194cfcb85ccd","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:26:48.875Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a91baeab8b45d5a0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
