rver-side configuration change that delegates artifact\n49\t  operations to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, per the mechanism and design\n50\t  selected by the routing-design investigation.\n51\t- Keep non-artifact operations (experiment tracking, model registry, prompt registry)\n52\t  unaffected by the delegation.\n53\t- Keep the configuration operator-managed where the mechanism allows (rendered from the\n54\t  MLflow CR), consistent with the split-server topology being declaratively configured.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- The tracking server delegates artifact operations to the dedicated artifacts-only\n59\t  instance per the selected design, verified by artifact requests reaching the dedicated\n60\t  instance and being subject to its workspace validation.\n61\t- Non-artifact operations continue to be served by the main tracking deployment unchanged.\n62\t- If gateway-level routing is found sufficient (branch A outcome), this epic is removed\n63\t  with no residual scope.\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated\n68\t  artifacts-only instance — conditional contribution in branch B, alongside the\n69\t  operator-managed routing configuration.\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf9976110f823b6f","agent_id":"a384cf149fdbd7daa","session_id":"40ac0a95-f7b4-4f3c-bf55-b2c4e97b3f62","uuid":"cc0dc5f9-450d-47dd-9f17-a2767774dc90","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:30:50.087Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9acc99491a537266","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
