{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b29a0f20c0f0b5a9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n3\ttitle: Validate plugin workspace-resolution independence from tracking store initialization\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 1\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: High\n19\tai_implementability_score: 3\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Validate plugin workspace-resolution independence from tracking store initialization\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves the strategy's open question: does workspace store\n30\tinitialization and workspace resolution in the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` auth plugin\n31\tdepend on tracking store (or model registry store) availability? The plugin, registered\n32\tthrough the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group and loaded by\n33\t`WorkspaceStoreRegistry`, already provides experiment-to-workspace mapping for the tracking\n34\tserver's non-artifact operations. The workspace-aware artifacts-only server requires that\n35\tsame resolution to function in a context where tracking and model registry stores are not\n36\tinitialized. The answer determines the scope of the plugin extension work: verification\n37\tonly, or a refactor that factors workspace resolution into an independent initialization\n38\tpath. It also validates the strategy assumption that the `kubernetes://` workspace store\n39\tprovides experiment-to-workspace mapping accessible without initializing tracking stores.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Analyze the plugin's initialization path: entry-point loading via\n44\t  `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`, workspace store construction for the `kubernetes://` URI\n45\t  scheme, and any transitive dependencies on tracking store or model registry store\n46\t  initialization.\n47\t- Identify every coupling point between workspace resolution and full tracking server\n48\t  initialization (imports, module-level state, store lookups, configuration reads).\n49\t- Determine whether the workspace store itself (independent of the plugin) can resolve\n50\t  experiment-to-workspace mappings without a tracking store.\n51\t- If coupling exists, produce a concrete refactor plan that factors workspace resolution\n52\t  into an independent initialization path within the plugin, preserving the existing\n53\t  behavior for the tracking server's non-artifact operations.\n54\t- Deliver a findings document with a definitive coupled / not-coupled answer and, if\n55\t  coupled, the refactor plan that the plugin extension work will execute.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- A findings document states definitively whether the plugin's workspace resolution\n60\t  functions with tracking and model registry stores uninitialized, citing the specific\n61\t  initialization code paths examined.\n62\t- If coupled: the refactor plan lists each coupling point and the proposed independent\n63\t  initialization path, sufficient for the plugin extension work to be scoped and\n64\t  estimated.\n65\t- If not coupled: the answer is demonstrated by exercising workspace resolution in an\n66\t  artifacts-only-style context (stores uninitialized) with a pass/fail result recorded.\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- HLR-7 (auth plugin workspace resolution in the artifacts-only context): this\n71\t  investigation determines that requirement's implementation scope.\n72\t- Enables HLR-1, HLR-2, HLR-3: the server-side workspace validation depends on plugin\n73\t  resolution functioning store-free.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b17cdad35f3ebf26","agent_id":"a0c833f15853879fd","session_id":"40ac0a95-f7b4-4f3c-bf55-b2c4e97b3f62","uuid":"525cea02-1696-4c5b-a24d-0b24cb638afe","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:31:59.636Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b29a0f20c0f0b5a9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
