{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a19d4e2883e16bb6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E006\n3\ttitle: Operator deployment of the dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: The HTTPRoute design for the dedicated instance follows the routing\n15\t    approach selected by the investigation; if routing is handled server-side, the\n16\t    HTTPRoute scope of this epic changes accordingly.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 1\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 6\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Operator deployment of the dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis epic delivers the operator's split-server topology for the artifacts-only instance:\n39\tthe MLflow operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance as a separate\n40\tDeployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute, distinct from the main tracking Deployment\n41\t(Staff Engineer input: this is a split deployment, not a configuration toggle). The\n42\toperator propagates workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`,\n43\t`--workspace-store-uri`, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) to the artifacts-only instance\n44\tusing the same configuration mechanisms it already uses for the main tracking deployment,\n45\tand deploys the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar identically. Users configure a single MLflow CR;\n46\tthe operator manages the split topology declaratively.\n47\t\n48\t## Scope\n49\t\n50\t- New Helm chart templates (within the operator's existing Helm-in-operator pattern) for\n51\t  the artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute, rendered from the MLflow CR spec\n52\t  and applied via Server-Side Apply like the main tracking deployment's resources.\n53\t- Propagate the workspace-aware flag combination to the artifacts-only instance:\n54\t  `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name\n55\t  kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts`.\n56\t- Deploy the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar on the artifacts-only instance identically to the main\n57\t  tracking deployment (authentication layer unchanged).\n58\t- Create the artifacts-only instance's HTTPRoute conditionally based on runtime Gateway API\n59\t  CRD discovery, consistent with the operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies.\n60\t- Operator validation: reject MLflow CR configurations that enable the split artifacts-only\n61\t  instance without the workspace flags, so misconfiguration cannot result in artifact\n62\t  requests bypassing workspace validation (risk mitigation from the strategy).\n63\t- Verify the operator's Helm chart rendering supports the second Deployment without\n64\t  structural changes to the chart architecture (strategy assumption).\n65\t\n66\t## Acceptance Criteria\n67\t\n68\t- Given an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled, when the operator\n69\t  reconciles the CR, then it creates a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and\n70\t  HTTPRoute separate from the main tracking Deployment, measured by the presence of\n71\t  distinct Deployment resources with the correct flag combinations.\n72\t- The artifacts-only Deployment's container command runs with `--artifacts-only\n73\t  --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth\n74\t  --serve-artifacts`, measured by inspecting the container command in the rendered\n75\t  Deployment spec.\n76\t- The operator rejects (with a clear validation error) configurations that enable the\n77\t  dedicated artifacts-only instance without the workspace flags.\n78\t- The HTTPRoute for the artifacts-only instance is created only when the Gateway API CRD\n79\t  is present at runtime, consistent with the operator's conditional discovery pattern.\n80\t\n81\t## HLR Traceability\n82\t\n83\t- HLR-5 (P1): operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment\n84\t  with its own Service and HTTPRoute — direct coverage.\n85\t\n86\t## Risks / Notes\n87\t\n88\t- The HTTPRoute design follows the routing-design investigation's selected approach; if\n89\t  that outcome changes the ingress design, this epic's HTTPRoute scope is rewritten\n90\t  accordingly.\n91\t- The rendered flag combination references the server-side composability capability; this\n92\t  epic's deliverable is the rendered Deployment spec, which is verifiable independently —\n93\t  end-to-end behavior is validated in the integration validation work.\n94\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b17cdad35f3ebf26","agent_id":"a0c833f15853879fd","session_id":"40ac0a95-f7b4-4f3c-bf55-b2c4e97b3f62","uuid":"b13ac5e3-f84c-46ec-a1d0-290bef76d709","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:32:06.164Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a19d4e2883e16bb6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
