{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-80de9c37160689aa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E007\n3\ttitle: Operator configuration of artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: Implements the routing mechanism selected by the investigation;\n15\t    gateway-level path routing versus server-side delegation change the implementation\n16\t    surface of this epic.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 1\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 5\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Operator configuration of artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis epic delivers the second half of the operator's split-server topology: configuring\n39\tthe main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only\n40\tinstance, implementing the routing mechanism selected by the routing-design investigation\n41\t(gateway-level HTTPRoute routing and/or main-deployment configuration updates). The main\n42\ttracking server continues to handle experiment tracking, model registry, and prompt\n43\tregistry; artifact serving is delegated to the dedicated instance with workspace\n44\tvalidation. The routing is managed declaratively from the single MLflow CR so users do not\n45\tmanage individual resources.\n46\t\n47\t## Scope\n48\t\n49\t- Implement the routing mechanism selected by the routing-design investigation for\n50\t  directing artifact traffic from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated\n51\t  artifacts-only instance.\n52\t- Update the main tracking Deployment's configuration as determined by that design (for\n53\t  example, routing configuration rendered into the main deployment's resources).\n54\t- If the investigation selects the branch requiring a tracking-server-side delegation\n55\t  configuration change, that server-side work is planned as the conditional follow-up\n56\t  identified by the investigation; this epic covers the operator-managed routing\n57\t  configuration.\n58\t- Keep the routing configuration declarative: derived from the MLflow CR via the operator's\n59\t  Helm-in-operator rendering, not manually managed resources.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- Given an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled, the rendered operator\n64\t  configuration routes artifact traffic from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated\n65\t  artifacts-only instance, per the mechanism selected by the routing-design investigation.\n66\t- The routing configuration is rendered declaratively from the MLflow CR (no\n67\t  manually-managed intermediate resources).\n68\t- Artifact requests entering through the main tracking deployment's ingress reach the\n69\t  dedicated artifacts-only instance and are subject to its workspace validation, verified\n70\t  end-to-end once the dedicated instance deployment and the workspace-aware server\n71\t  capability are available.\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated\n76\t  artifacts-only instance — direct coverage (together with the conditional server-side\n77\t  delegation work if the routing-design investigation selects that branch).\n78\t\n79\t## Risks / Notes\n80\t\n81\t- The implementation surface depends on the routing-design outcome; this epic is gated by\n82\t  that investigation with a rewrite impact.\n83\t- Coordination with the dedicated-instance deployment work is required where both modify\n84\t  the operator's Helm chart (merge-conflict risk, not a dependency).\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b17cdad35f3ebf26","agent_id":"a0c833f15853879fd","session_id":"40ac0a95-f7b4-4f3c-bf55-b2c4e97b3f62","uuid":"7a638c85-98cf-46b4-8dd8-accad7431c06","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:32:06.772Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-80de9c37160689aa","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
