ia\n47\t\n48\t- A decision record states the selected audit channel with rationale and PM/Security\n49\t  sign-off.\n50\t- The audit event content requirements (identifiers, context, volume expectations) are\n51\t  defined well enough to scope the audit logging implementation.\n52\t\n53\t## HLR Traceability\n54\t\n55\t- HLR-8 (P2): audit logging for workspace access denials in artifact serving — this\n56\t  investigation determines that requirement's scope and channel.\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b17cdad35f3ebf26","agent_id":"a0c833f15853879fd","session_id":"40ac0a95-f7b4-4f3c-bf55-b2c4e97b3f62","uuid":"163cc895-786e-45fc-ae18-eea3e9616446","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:32:07.374Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a04db5bab3a5e753","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
