t content\n49\t  requirements defined by the audit-channel decision.\n50\t- Implement the selected channel (server log output by default per the strategy's\n51\t  requirement; OTLP or Kubernetes audit log if the decision selects otherwise).\n52\t- Ensure audit logging does not alter the fail-closed denial behavior itself (logging is\n53\t  observational, not gating).\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- Workspace access denials in artifact serving produce audit records through the selected\n58\t  channel, containing the identifiers and context defined by the audit-channel decision.\n59\t- Denial behavior (HTTP 403 for non-membership, fail-closed denial when the workspace store\n60\t  is unreachable) is unchanged by the addition of audit logging.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-8 (P2): audit logging for workspace access denials in artifact serving through server\n65\t  logs — direct coverage (channel per the audit-channel decision).\n66\t\n67\t## Risks / Notes\n68\t\n69\t- Scope depends on the audit-channel decision; this epic is gated by that investigation\n70\t  with a rewrite impact. The strategy's requirement text specifies server logs, so that is\n71\t  the default scope unless the decision selects a telemetry channel.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b17cdad35f3ebf26","agent_id":"a0c833f15853879fd","session_id":"40ac0a95-f7b4-4f3c-bf55-b2c4e97b3f62","uuid":"7cccabf9-642a-4893-867e-4e16d296df6e","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:32:10.810Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d0ba1b0d82fc371","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
